<title>USA: First Virtual Q1 shr loss widens to $0.39.</title>
<headline>First Virtual Q1 shr loss widens to $0.39.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Virtual Holdings Incorporated</p>
<p>				Statements of Operations</p>
<p>						Three months ended</p>
<p>				     Mar 31,	 Dec 31,    Mar 31,</p>
<p>					 1997	    1996	 1996</p>
<p> Revenues			 $392,917	$197,604  $244,466*</p>
<p> Cost of revenues		111,514	  47,104     92,510</p>
<p> Gross margin		    281,403	 150,500    151,956</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>  Marketing and sales	1,049,337     1,091,539    156,476</p>
<p>Research, development and</p>
<p>   engineering		 1,452,006     2,332,911    332,531</p>
<p>General and administrative</p>
<p>				   1,163,581     1,267,819    484,356</p>
<p> Total operating expenses  3,664,924     4,692,269    973,363</p>
<p> EBITDA			(3,383,521)   (4,541,769)  (821,407)</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>  amortization		   257,999	 226,743     54,554</p>
<p> Loss from operations    (3,641,520)   (4,768,512)  (875,961)</p>
<p>Interest income (expense),</p>
<p>  net				167,947	  58,886	1,036</p>
<p> Net loss		    (3,473,573)   (4,709,626)  (874,925)</p>
<p> Net loss per share	     (0.39)	  (0.54)     (0.11)</p>
<p>Shares used in per share</p>
<p>  computation	     8,795,323 **     8,769,491  8,257,260</p>
<p>* Beginning in July 1996, the Company instituted annual renewal fees and began to recognize revenues from Buyer and Seller registration and renewal fees over a twelve month period.  Prior to July 1996, revenues from registration fees were recognized in the month the registration fee was processed and the VirtualPIN was issued.  As of March 31, 1997, deferred revenue was $776,505.</p>
<p>** Shares used in computing net loss per share for the quarter ended March 31, 1997 excludes the warrants held by First USA Merchant Services to purchase 1,328,006 shares of common stock at an exercise price of $0.01 per share.  Had the shares associated with these warrants been outstanding, the net loss per share for the quarter ended March 31, 1997 would have been $0.34. These warrants were included in the pro forma net loss per share in 1996 pursuant to the requirements of the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
